Effective date: October 24, 2026

Copyright (c) 2026 PT NAKAFA TEKNO KREATIF. All rights reserved.

Nakafa is source available. It is not open source, and it is not free to
reuse. The source is public for one reason: so that anyone can read it, audit
it, and understand how Nakafa works. It is not public so that anyone can copy
it, fork it, rebrand it, publish it, or gain anything from it.

By reading, cloning, downloading, forking, running, or otherwise using Nakafa,
you accept this license. If you do not accept it, do not use Nakafa.

## 1. Definitions

`Nakafa` means the software in this repository, in the Aksara repository, and
in every earlier version of them: source code, build files, configuration,
scripts, database schema, prompts, tests, documentation, user interface,
design, and the material the software produces or the official services serve.

`Official services` means `https://nakafa.com`, its subdomains, and the
official Nakafa apps and APIs.

`You` means the person or entity that receives, reads, or uses Nakafa.

`Benefit` means any advantage, with or without money, for you or for anyone
else. It includes revenue, payment, salary, sponsorship, advertising or
affiliate income, donations, grants, prizes, followers, subscribers, views,
likes, audience growth, attention, virality, reputation, portfolio or career
value, hiring, investment, traffic, leads, data, and any product or
competitive advantage. These are not a Benefit: learning that stays private to
one person; a grade, score, or certificate that a school, university, or exam
body gives you for your own work; and submitting a contribution to an official
Nakafa repository under `.github/CONTRIBUTING.md`, with the public record of
that submission.

`Personal private use` means use by one natural person, alone, for that
person's own learning, audit, or evaluation, that produces no Benefit and is
not done for, shown to, or shared with any employer, client, school,
organization, team, community, channel, or social media account. Using the
official services with your own account under their terms is personal private
use.

`Publish` means to make something available to, or perceivable by, anyone other
than you, by any means. It includes repositories, forks, mirrors, archives,
packages, releases, hosted or deployed instances whether public or private,
screenshots, recordings, live streams, videos, posts, articles, courses,
slides, talks, demos, datasets, and output of AI systems.

`Copy` means a reproduction of Nakafa in whole or in part, or a modified
version, translation, port, or reimplementation that reproduces Nakafa's code
or content, whether made by hand or with AI tools. Ideas, methods, and
functions are not protected by this license; work that does not reproduce
Nakafa's code or content is not a copy, even if it covers the same subject.

`Written permission` means a written agreement signed by an authorized
representative of PT NAKAFA TEKNO KREATIF, or a written approval sent from the
official address in Section 15 that names you and the exact use it allows. A
written permission given before the effective date stays valid for the use it
covers.

## 2. Scope

This license applies to Nakafa unless a license file names a different license
for a file. It does not apply to:

- Third-party dependencies, packages, services, fonts, and libraries, which keep
  their own licenses.
- Educational content, articles, exercises, explanations, datasets, copy,
  images, video, audio, and other non-code material, which `CONTENT_LICENSE.md`
  covers.
- The Nakafa name, logos, domains, product names, mascot, characters, and visual
  identity, which `TRADEMARKS.md` covers.

All rights that this license does not expressly grant are reserved by
PT NAKAFA TEKNO KREATIF.

## 3. What You May Do

Without written permission, you may do only the following:

- Use the official services under their terms.
- Read, view, inspect, audit, and study the source code, including how it works,
  only within personal private use.
- Keep one copy of Nakafa, plus any backup copy that applicable law lets you
  make, run it, and change it, only within personal private use.
- Ask an AI system to explain or review Nakafa that you lawfully have, for your
  own personal private use, with a setting that does not keep or train on your
  input where your provider offers one, without publishing the output.
- Create a fork on GitHub only to prepare and submit a pull request to an
  official Nakafa repository. The fork may not be used for anything else: no
  releases, packages, pages, deployments, promotion, or independent
  development. Delete it within 7 days after the pull request is merged or
  closed, and in any case when it has had no open pull request for 14 days.
  GitHub's terms let any user create a fork of a public repository; this
  license grants no other right in that fork.
- Report security issues privately as `SECURITY.md` describes, and open issues
  and pull requests under `.github/CONTRIBUTING.md`, without pasting Nakafa's
  code into them beyond the lines needed to show the problem.
- Mention Nakafa by name and link to an official repository or to
  `https://nakafa.com`, truthfully, without reproducing Nakafa, as
  `TRADEMARKS.md` allows.

These permissions are personal, limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, and
non-sublicensable.

## 4. What Is Forbidden

Everything that Section 3 does not list is forbidden without written
permission. In particular, you may not:

- Publish Nakafa or any copy, in whole or in part.
- Fork, mirror, redistribute, package, sublicense, sell, rent, lend, host, or
  deploy Nakafa or any copy, for anyone, including on a private network or for
  a team, school, or organization.
- Rebrand, rename, or white-label Nakafa or any copy, or present it as your own
  work, as someone else's work, or as a new or independent project.
- Use Nakafa or any copy to obtain any Benefit, for you or for anyone else,
  except the search and answer use that `CONTENT_LICENSE.md` Section 4 allows.
- Use Nakafa's code, content, structure, or output, or anything you learned
  from them, in any work shown to or shared with anyone other than you,
  including an explanation, review, walkthrough, tutorial, talk, slide deck,
  course, quiz, lesson, or rewritten text, whether or not it copies the words
  or code.
- Use Nakafa for or within any employer, client, school, organization, team,
  community, product, service, course, competition, hackathon, channel, or
  account, other than your own use of the official services.
- Show, record, stream, or post Nakafa's source code, your copy, your changed
  version, or their screens or output.
- Train, fine-tune, evaluate, or benchmark an AI model with Nakafa; build a
  dataset, embedding store, or retrieval index from it; have an AI system or
  another person rewrite, translate, port, or reimplement Nakafa from your
  reading of it; or give Nakafa to an AI system except as Section 3 allows.
- Remove, hide, or change any copyright, license, attribution, source, or
  brand notice.
- Get around any access control or technical protection of the official
  services.

